    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Act 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The latest in Christine Molloy and Joe Lawlor’s series of cinematic essays is a rich and thought-provoking journey through ageing, legacy and the intersection between artistic and personal relationships."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/elsinore-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Elsinore"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Andrew Scott is a towering presence in this singular account of Ian Charleson’s life, capturing the moment when he faced his own mortality as he prepared to play Hamlet at the Royal National Theatre."
    },
    {
      "type": "image",
      "url": "https://d3cyv0xf0ss37v.cloudfront.net/2026/films/560x315/we-were-here-01.jpeg",
      "alt": "",
      "caption": "",
      "credit": "BFI London Film Festival 2026"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The Man I Love: Remembering the AIDS Crisis"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "This event gives space for remembrance and reflection on the legacy and lasting impact of the AIDS epidemic."
    }
  ]
